00:05:19.310 --> 00:05:21.020
Some of them come with inherent dangers.

00:05:21.020 --> 00:05:25.060
But these women are doing courageous work
without hesitation.

00:05:25.060 --> 00:05:28.150
Nic Robertson has more.

00:05:28.150 --> 00:05:35.110
&gt;&gt; Reporter: In a man's world, War is changing
everything.

00:05:35.110 --> 00:05:44.280
Tatiana is at the vanguard, shattering Ukrainian
coal mining history, a woman on her way to

00:05:44.280 --> 00:05:46.830
work 1,000 feet underground.

00:05:46.830 --> 00:05:50.490
Normal, it is okay now?

00:05:50.490 --> 00:05:51.490
&gt;&gt; Yes.

00:05:51.490 --> 00:05:53.420
&gt;&gt; You like it?

00:05:53.420 --> 00:05:55.610
&gt;&gt; I love it.

00:05:55.610 --> 00:05:56.610
&gt;&gt; You wanted to be a miner.

00:05:56.610 --> 00:05:57.610
&gt;&gt; Yes.

00:05:57.610 --> 00:05:58.610
[5:30:06 AM]

00:05:58.610 --> 00:05:59.610
&gt;&gt; Yes.

00:05:59.610 --> 00:06:01.129
&gt;&gt; Your family, your grandfather, your father
was a miner.

00:06:01.129 --> 00:06:02.360
&gt;&gt; Yeah.

00:06:02.360 --> 00:06:05.949
&gt;&gt; Reporter: She used to work above ground.

00:06:05.949 --> 00:06:11.650
But when miners got called up to fight and
martial law cleared women for dangerous job,

00:06:11.650 --> 00:06:15.780
she jumped at a job team in the mine.

00:06:15.780 --> 00:06:19.030
&gt;&gt; Translator: I always wanted to work here.

00:06:19.030 --> 00:06:21.229
But girls were not allowed.

00:06:21.229 --> 00:06:25.220
When many men were constricted, the mine had
to keep working.

00:06:25.220 --> 00:06:28.399
So to protect our country, the girls stepped
up.

00:06:28.399 --> 00:06:33.520
&gt;&gt; Reporter: She works six hour shifts, three
days on, one day off.

00:06:33.520 --> 00:06:35.690
Earns more than previously.

00:06:35.690 --> 00:06:39.490
And wants to keep her underground job when
the war is over.

00:06:39.490 --> 00:06:41.780
&gt;&gt; Translator: My work is not physically difficult.

00:06:41.780 --> 00:06:43.669
I like it a lot.

00:06:43.669 --> 00:06:46.039
I would like to continue working here.

00:06:46.039 --> 00:06:54.199
&gt;&gt; Reporter: In this bastion of male dominated
tradition, that may not be so easy.

00:06:54.199 --> 00:07:00.020
&gt;&gt; Translator: I think when the war is over
and when we win, I think women will return

00:07:00.020 --> 00:07:01.020
above

00:07:01.020 --> 00:07:02.020
[5:31:08 AM]

00:07:02.020 --> 00:07:03.120
think women will return above the ground and
do woman's jobs.

00:07:03.120 --> 00:07:10.050
&gt;&gt; Reporter: Yesterday even this chief engineer
admits without Tatiana and many other women,

00:07:10.050 --> 00:07:15.110
the mine could not have kept going.

00:07:15.110 --> 00:07:21.240
&gt;&gt; Our miners got called up to fight and our
women wanted to help the mine and the country.

00:07:21.240 --> 00:07:25.669
So far 46 women are working under the ground
now.

00:07:25.669 --> 00:07:34.479
&gt;&gt; Reporter: There is plenty of traditional
male only workplaces are finding women stepping

00:07:34.479 --> 00:07:42.020
up and taking jobs that before the war would
have only gone to men.

00:07:42.020 --> 00:07:44.020
Maria is among them.

00:07:44.020 --> 00:07:47.300
For the love of Ukraine and of her husband.

00:07:47.300 --> 00:07:53.029
&gt;&gt; Translator: I knew the theory but the practice
turned out to be a little harder.

00:07:53.029 --> 00:07:59.099
&gt;&gt; Reporter: She took up his blacksmith job
when he got called up to fight last year.

00:07:59.099 --> 00:08:01.540
They bought the forge together a few years
earlier, invested

00:08:01.540 --> 00:08:02.540
[5:32:09 AM]

00:08:02.540 --> 00:08:05.249
few years earlier, invested their future in
it.

00:08:05.249 --> 00:08:09.479
&gt;&gt; Translator: This is my husband's passion
and his life's business.

00:08:09.479 --> 00:08:13.979
I decided to support him to keep his job alive
while he is serving.

00:08:13.979 --> 00:08:21.039
&gt;&gt; Reporter: She shows me a video of her husband
Andre working at the same anvil pre-war, his

00:08:21.039 --> 00:08:24.030
artwork selling in the U.S.

00:08:24.030 --> 00:08:32.829
And Europe for hundreds ofe she is focusing
on simpler stuff.

00:08:32.829 --> 00:08:38.019
&gt;&gt; Translator: I very often cry in the forge
here.

00:08:38.019 --> 00:08:41.979
My husband is defending us and it is very
dangerous.

00:08:41.979 --> 00:08:45.690
But this work helps me to hold on and not
fall apart.

00:08:45.690 --> 00:08:48.610
&gt;&gt; Reporter: Women have been here before.

00:08:48.610 --> 00:08:51.330
Remember Rosie the riveter?

00:08:51.330 --> 00:08:54.580
Icon of women at work in world War II.

00:08:54.580 --> 00:08:58.839
She and others cracked the glass ceiling.

00:08:58.839 --> 00:09:03.000
More than a hint of Rosie in Maria and perhaps
of changes

00:09:03.000 --> 00:09:04.000
[5:33:10 AM]

00:09:04.000 --> 00:09:05.000
Maria and perhaps of changes here too.

00:09:05.000 --> 00:09:07.620
&gt;&gt; Translator: It is tiring work but interesting.

00:09:07.620 --> 00:09:11.459
I would like to do it when I feel like it,
not when I have to do it.

00:09:11.459 --> 00:09:19.870
&gt;&gt; Reporter: Maria, Tatiana, two of many who
bravely stepped up no doubt more challenges

00:09:19.870 --> 00:09:25.820
ahead.

